  {
   "key": "0x01",
   "name": "control A",
   "access": "write",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
     "lines": "490-491"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
     "lines": "553-560"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
     "lines": "561-567"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
     "lines": "568-572"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
     "lines": "693-697"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
     "function": "pia6821_device::write",
     "case": [
      "0x01"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
     "function": "pia6821_device::control_a_w"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
     "function": "pia6821_device::set_out_ca2"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bits 3, 4 and 5 of the two control registers control the CA2 and CB2 lines, deciding whether a line is an interrupt input or an output control signal.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
       "lines": "568-572",
       "sha": "11205b4f9f5d335ff9dd59c52039bec1a39f30b6ccec88c5961ff86647ea8a05"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bit 2 is stored; the text says a 1 gives access to the peripheral register and a 0 addresses the Data Direction Register.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
       "lines": "555-560",
       "sha": "f40515fb5059efc8344f6232a47d93a0ddf421d311dcfa22e7ca38c13e5c8c08"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The interrupt flag bits cannot be set directly from the MPU data bus.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
       "lines": "561-567",
       "sha": "c64d8aa086dd721d42b3c319f911d32cb6c0551a9df23323c392a22430a41468"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The function of this signal line is programmed with Control Register A.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
       "lines": "490-491",
       "sha": "13507a67ef61e0d2206f50a9cc06fe7eeb23bcfdaa5977c1a7f773d4d411d779"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In set/reset mode CA2 goes low as the MPU writes bit 3 = 0 into the control register and high as it writes bit 3 = 1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC6821.raw.txt",
       "lines": "693-697",
       "sha": "b4815a1ac578e3958c0dd24f85eac9ab9410f4dda6bf79165900f62ffcb61760"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "In strobe output mode a control write drives CA2 high when CA2 was not an output or is low.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "755-760",
       "sha": "99ea3a3654cd24b921e1c509ae071c88f5c00af7fcc0420277034127ca17f190"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "When bit 5 changes from output to input, MAME drives CA2 high through its output handler.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "742",
       "sha": "4fb9d3a5341243627cf5122cc0c79259d6cecb2641aa2281a0b4bc9e8ee8ece6"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "746",
       "sha": "44b672e48006815d5d395f0c1391009c3ed76da130d775eb75847dd738f43027"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "762-767",
       "sha": "2de4f02fe44a3e1846094723a060d86b69c57ee90d0f2f48a71e1d54eb1a9682"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "1118",
       "sha": "2fa653261170f2370c69c619fae2ffa3fc6b9375d03ae1db4c248d29cbca385a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With no output handler set, MAME only remembers that a value is pending and logs a warning if the next one overwrites it.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/6821pia.cpp",
       "lines": "348-354",
       "sha": "35f461f51d61c3decde56033d700f78437f00be22df99aeaf97b085e3548d347"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
